            "review_title": "Review at Blue Restaurant",
            "review_text": "MaxYourLife\nUnited States282 contributions\n1\nExcellent seafood fried rice\nDec 2018 • Couples\nHubby and I both had the seafood fried rice (sfr) which our server recommended. Hubby said it was the best he had in a long time. I was afraid it would come out with all sorts of weird things on it, but pleasantly surprised at the shrimp and maybe squid pieces chopped up with cucumber and carrots. We both thought it was delicious. We also started with the Vietnamese spring rolls (Vsr) fried and a sweet taste—coconut milk maybe? I don’t know but they were also very good. We would get both dishes again. \nCrabmeat and mushroom soup had an egg drop base, which hubby doesn’t like so he just picked out the mushroom pieces and had those with his fried rice. \nVery inexpensive for big portion sizes. Sfr was 80k Dong, Vsr was 30k I think. 1 Water and 2 cokes were 20k each. All in all it came to 330k. Server was sweet and didn’t speak much English but entire menu is in English, and she was thrilled at 30k tip. \nNice view of water and slight breeze with shade.\nRead more\nWritten December 23, 2018\nBlue Restaurant\nThank you very much for your comments and comments. Blue restaurant hope welcomes you and serves you the next time. Hope to bring more delicious and attractive new dishes for you!\nRead more\nWritten December 24, 2018\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
